    <string name="settings_omap_legend_title">Map colours (IOF)</string>
    <string name="settings_omap_legend_white">White — Normal open forest. Easy to run through.</string>
    <string name="settings_omap_legend_green">Green — Dense vegetation. Darker green means harder to push through.</string>
    <string name="settings_omap_legend_yellow">Yellow — Open land, fields, clearings, or meadows.</string>
    <string name="settings_omap_legend_brown">Brown — Landforms (contour lines, hills, pits, earth banks).</string>
    <string name="settings_omap_legend_black">Black — Rock features (cliffs, boulders) and man-made objects (paths, fences, buildings).</string>
    <string name="settings_omap_legend_purple">Purple / magenta — The race course (triangle = start, circles = controls, double circle = finish).</string>
    <string name="settings_omap_legend_note">Pseud-O approximates these colours from OpenStreetMap. Surveyed ISOM (forest) and ISSprOM (sprint) maps are drawn with OCAD or OpenOrienteering Mapper — OrienteerRun does not embed those editors.</string>
